Z||000007||contra||07-14-2000||09:58 AM||||one last question i guess<BR>do i hafta take the engine out of my car to install this thing?<BR>also, how come some people charge up to $3000 for installing a turbo charger when you can buy one used and then pay somebody to install it for under a grand?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||turbo86se||07-14-2000||11:21 AM||||Contra, I assume you're talking about the turbo kits such as MillerWoods and Design One that IRM and Fiero Plus offers. They cost this much because they include everything you could possibly need to install the unit in your Fiero. Everything is custom made to fit a Fiero. It's a plug and play kit. IMHO it's worth every penny, and there's rarely an instance where I get out of my Fiero without a smile on my face!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||turbo86se||07-14-2000||12:15 PM||||Oh yeah, contra, if you need more info, I've got 5 pages of info from Fiero News, where they got into detail about the turbo, how it works, and what to expect. Let me know if you'd like a copy.||||reg||1
Z||000010||contra||07-14-2000||01:07 PM||||yeah send all the info you have to my email address<BR>a_kalicak@hotmail.com<P>thanx<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||07-14-2000||02:06 PM||||DEFINATELY BUY A COMPLETE KIT. I did for my car, didnt even have to buy a screw. kits have everything, even new exhaust crossover to mount the turbo, mine also came with special muffler and boost gauge for dash. Alls been fine for last 40k miles. for everyday use i use about 4 pnds boost, but ive had it up to 14 pnds||||reg||1
